  "findings": [
    "The original fixed host calls super.onCreate before constructing its WebView; the original event No WebView in onActivityCreated is consistent with the fixed AOSP ordering.",
    "New override delegates once to super.callActivityOnCreate first. The framework call finishes the actual onCreate override before returning; attachment then runs synchronously on the same lifecycle call, before the subsequent onStart/loadUrl path.",
    "Non-target activities still receive their normal superclass call, then return without attaching. Missing-WebView, existing-client, non-null URL and RuntimeException guards remain intact.",
    "created() now updates state only; it no longer probes the early unconstructed view. No duplicate startup attachment or second callback delegation is added.",
    "The actual compiled javap confirms invokespecial Instrumentation.callActivityOnCreate before target-only attachConsole. The owner actual JDK/D8, HeaderBudgetTest and unsigned aapt/apksigner logs were read, not rerun.",
    "Game APK, host, model, original SDK/driver/menu predicates, timeout budgets and all guarded source/package identities are unchanged. This fixes the diagnostic hook timing only, not the unobserved race graphics fault."
  ],
